# The agent realm, by hand
#
# Play through `blong-dev proxy` (it logs in and keeps the session), then run these in order:
#
#   blong-dev proxy --port 8099 --target http://localhost:8080 \
#       --username testAdmin --password testPassword
#
# A ticket is claimed before it can be run, and a question the agent asks is answered through
# `agent.answer.receive` — by its prompt id, so a retried click is safe.

@base = http://localhost:8099

### One pass of the worker: the inbox, then a claim
POST {{base}}/agent/worker/tick
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"workerId": "host-local", "engineAccount": "local"}}

### Take one ticket without running it
POST {{base}}/agent/ticket/claim
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"workerId": "host-local", "engineAccount": "local"}}

### What the realm recorded for a session
POST {{base}}/agent/session/get
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"sessionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"}}

### Run it, when the claim was made separately
POST {{base}}/agent/session/run
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"sessionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "workerId": "host-local"}}

### Answer the question it parked on
POST {{base}}/agent/answer/receive
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"promptId": "the-prompt-id-from-agent-session-get", "answerText": "the chosen fix"}}

### Close the ticket
POST {{base}}/agent/ticket/release
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"ticketId": "T-1001", "workerId": "host-local", "ticketStatus": "done"}}

### What this host left suspended, and what to do about it
POST {{base}}/agent/recovery/scan
content-type: application/json

{"params": {"workerId": "host-local"}}
